Package: tidysoilr
Title: Tidy Tools for Soil Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: Pipe-friendly tools for soil laboratory, profile and
    spectroscopy data. Covers USDA and FAO texture classes and log-ratio
    transforms of particle-size data, hydrometer and pipette particle-size
    analysis, bulk density, porosity and pedotransfer functions (Saxton and
    Rawls 2006 <doi:10.2136/sssaj2005.0117>), van Genuchten water retention
    fitting, equal-area quadratic splines for depth harmonisation (Bishop
    et al. 1999 <doi:10.1016/S0016-7061(99)00003-8>), organic carbon stocks,
    exchangeable bases, fertility ratings and nutrient indices, soil quality
    indices, and spectral preprocessing (standard normal variate,
    multiplicative scatter correction, Savitzky-Golay derivatives and
    continuum removal). Integrates with 'tidymodels' through 'recipes'
    steps, profile-grouped, spatial block and Kennard-Stone resampling for
    'rsample', 'yardstick' metrics and a partial least squares 'parsnip'
    model, with 'broom' and 'ggplot2' methods including a texture triangle.
    Profile and spectra tibble subclasses keep their metadata through
    'dplyr' verbs. All methods are written in base R.
